# Cloudflare Pages serves /assets/* with "max-age=14400" (4 hours) by default,
# and these files are not fingerprinted: index.html points at assets/site.js
# by a fixed name. The page's data, by contrast, is always current - it fetches
# .agent-schematics/marketplace.json from raw.githubusercontent at load time.
#
# That combination broke the site on 2026-09-19. The catalogue split renamed a
# key inside that JSON (#78), so a browser still holding the previous site.js
# read a key the data no longer had and the page failed soft: hero stat
# "0 schematics" and "No schematics published yet.", not an error. Reproduced
# against the live catalogue with the previous script - 0 cards, 0 hero count,
# empty state shown - while a fresh load of the same data rendered 5.
#
# Revalidating instead of caching for hours costs a 304 per asset and makes the
# page's code at least as fresh as the data it renders. index.html already
# revalidates (max-age=0, must-revalidate), so the HTML was never the problem.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
